      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Adding to the benefits here: some avatars have shaders that only use Spherical Harmonics for lighting via light probe data. Toggling a light source on/off requires enabling a light which contains direct lighting information but allows no ability for updating GI or shaders that rely on light probes. So dark areas will permanently show certain models dark forever, and videos can't influence contribution on GI without the requirement avatars and shaders use other systems.\n\nLight sources increase draw calls in forward rendering to every single material they touch because all materials must reference the light color+position and reprocess. But since GI with L2 spherical harmonics is already processed on virtually all avatars/shaders, adjusting light probes in Udon would have zero rendering impact, allowing greater dynamics for Quest and PC much more easily, much greater performance than light sources, greater accuracy in dynamic systems, and more flexibility in authoring dynamic lighting systems.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-10-12T19:48:47.924Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Baked light probes are the way that VRChat avatars are lit, period. Currently the only way of effecting them is through enlighten, a long depreciated system that's unrealistic to implement. \n\nVertex lights, LTCGI, light volumes are all unreliable ways of lighting a group of custom avatars, and none of them are supported by many default/fallback avatars. Pixel lights and Projectors have massive costs on performance. \n\nPlease find new ways of letting us manipulate and effect existing light probes/groups at runtime, since 100% of avatars sample that form of light",
